  <title>Database tools</title>

  <p>Each company's books are a PostgreSQL database.
  <guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Database tools</gui></guiseq> keeps
  the list of them on this computer. It also opens by itself when PyGtk
  Posting starts and cannot connect.</p>

  <section id="databases">
  <title>Databases</title>
  <p>The <gui>Databases</gui> tab lists the connections saved on this
  computer. Click a name to rename it.</p>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Open</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the selected company in a second copy of PyGtk Posting.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Set as default</gui></title>
    <p>Makes it the company PyGtk Posting opens when it starts.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Delete</gui></title>
    <p>Removes the connection from the list. The database itself is
    kept.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

  <section id="connection">
  <title>Adding a connection</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>On the <gui>Connection</gui> tab, type the <gui>Server</gui>,
    <gui>Port</gui>, <gui>Username</gui> and <gui>Password</gui> of the
    PostgreSQL server, and click <gui>Test connection</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To use a company that already exists, choose it under
    <gui>Existing database</gui> and click <gui>Save connection</gui>. To start
    new books, type a name under <gui>New database</gui> and click
    <gui>Create</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>Check <gui>Mobile</gui> for a connection over a slow link: less data is
  loaded, so some windows show less.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="backup">
  <title>Backup and restore</title>
  <p>On the <gui>Backup / restore</gui> tab, check the <gui>Server</gui>,
  <gui>Port</gui> and <gui>Username</gui>.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Choose the database and click <gui>Backup database</gui>. The
    backup is saved to the default backup path. The main window reminds you
    when a backup is due; see <link xref="settings#general"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To restore, type a <gui>Database name for restore</gui>, a new
    name so nothing is overwritten, and click <gui>Restore from file</gui> to
    choose the backup.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>The <gui>Postgres path(s)</gui> tab sets where the PostgreSQL backup and
  restore programs are, and the default backup path.</p>
  </section>

</page>
